        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 
          <b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b "> Description</b> 
        </entry> 
      </row></thead> 
    <tbody class="- topic/tbody "> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Type 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 2 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 0 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 0 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> TSE Hardware Unit Capability structure 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry colname="col1" class="- topic/entry "> Length 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2" class="- topic/entry "> 2 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 2 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> N 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Varies (16 + Size of device Scope structure) 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> Flags 
        </entry> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> 1 
        </entry> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> 4 
        </entry> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> 01h 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col5" class="- topic/entry "> Bit 0: Include_PCI_ALL If set the TSE engine includes all the PCIe devices in the specified segment. When there is multiple TSE capability reporting structures, this flag should only be set by the last TSCRS. Two TSCRS should not be setting this flag. If clear, this TSE only includes the ports in the specified segment as defined by the 'device scope' field. The device can be of any type as described by the 'Type' field. There can be more than 1 TCRS reported by BIOS with this flag set. BIOS needs to make sure that the devices in the device scope structure should not be linked to multiple TCRS. 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry colname="col5" class="- topic/entry "> Bit 2: Virtualizable: Supports SRIOV or SIOV 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Bit 3: If Bit 2 is set, 0 = SRIOV, 1 = SIOV. if BIT2 is not set, Bit 3 should be 0 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Reserved 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 5 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 00h 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Reserved 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Segment Number 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 2 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 6 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 0000h 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> The PCI Segment associated with this unit 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> TSE Key Sources Supported 
        </entry> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> 1 
        </entry> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> 8 
        </entry> 
        <entry morerows="2" class="- topic/entry "> IA32_TSE_CAPABILITY. TSESSSS_ENGINE_KEY_SOURCE_SUPPORTED 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col5" class="- topic/entry "> Bit 0: CPU ISA 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry colname="col5" class="- topic/entry "> Bit 1: Security Controller 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Bit 2: Key engine inside TSE Engine 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> TSE Encryption Algorithm Supported 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 2 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 9 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> IA32_TSE_CAPABILITY. AES_XTS_256 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> BIT0: AES_XTS_256 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> TSE MAX Keys Supported 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 2 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 11 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> IA32_TSE _CAPABILITY. TSE_MAX_KEYS 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Indicates the maximum number of keys which are available. 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> TSE MAX BDFs supported 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 1 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 13 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> 
          <u class="+ topic/ph hi-d/u "> TSE_</u> IOCCE_Capability. MaxBdfSupported 
        </entry> 
        <entry class="- topic/entry "> Maximum number of devices this engine can support. This is the maximum number of NVMe drives that can be configured in the TSE engine to enable encryption. 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row class="- topic/row "> 
